{
  "package": "regexp",
  "notes": "regexp: Go 1.27 semantics (leftmost-first; leftmost-longest for POSIX and Longest), linear time, on Go's three matchers chosen as Go's find does: one-pass, the bit-state backtracker, and the Pike VM. nil slices become Option or an empty Vec, unmatched groups are None (-1 in submatch index vectors), single matches are (start, end) tuples, readers take RuneReader/Utf8RuneReader over io::Read. patterns are &str, so invalid-UTF-8 patterns cannot be passed. Additions without a Go symbol: find_index_at and find_submatch_index_at expose the search from an offset that Go runs internally (FindAll), and find_anchored_index_at and find_anchored_submatch_index_at accept only a match beginning at the offset.",
